我是说，主要是英版《办公室》。

158
00:07:13.840 --> 00:07:16.660
So, I was, I had been a huge fan since the British office.
所以，我从英版《办公室》开始就是它的超级粉丝了。

159
00:07:17.200 --> 00:07:23.900
So, for me, it felt very, like, full circle and neat for me personally just to, like, get to be on the show.
所以对我来说，能参演这部剧感觉就像是一个圆满的闭环，真的很棒。

160
00:07:24.660 --> 00:07:24.940
Yeah.
是啊。

161
00:07:25.100 --> 00:07:27.780
So, that was, I mean, it was, yeah, it was not a lot of deliberation or anything.
所以，我是说，真的，没怎么犹豫，一点都没有。

162
00:07:27.800 --> 00:07:29.640
I was like, of course, I would love to be on The Office.
我当时就想，当然了，我太想参演《办公室》了。

163
00:07:29.900 --> 00:07:31.340
What a great phone call to get.
能接到这样的电话真是太好了。

164
00:07:31.500 --> 00:07:31.740
Yeah.
是啊。

165
00:07:32.380 --> 00:07:32.660
Yeah.
没错。

166
00:07:32.800 --> 00:07:34.240
I haven't had a phone call that good in a while.
我已经很久没接到过这么好的电话了。

167
00:07:34.360 --> 00:07:34.480
Yeah.
是啊。

168
00:07:34.600 --> 00:07:35.180
That was a good one.
那确实是个好消息。

169
00:07:42.660 --> 00:07:47.260
Did they tell you at the time, oh, you're going to be paired with this other new guy?
他们当时有没有告诉你，哦，你要和另一个新人搭档？

170
00:07:47.460 --> 00:07:48.900
Did they give you any of those details?
他们有没有给你透露过这些细节？

171
00:07:49.240 --> 00:07:51.520
I knew we were going to be paired with another new guy.
我知道我会和另一个新人搭档。

172
00:07:51.880 --> 00:07:58.380
As far as, like, you know, the characterization, I don't recall there being a lot of specific notes about, like, how to play.
至于角色塑造方面，我不记得他们给过什么具体的表演指导。

173
00:07:58.460 --> 00:07:59.800
I mean, I think it was sort of like.
我是说，我觉得大概就是那样。

174
00:08:00.420 --> 00:08:01.380
Like, do your thing?
就像是，做你自己？

175
00:08:01.380 --> 00:08:03.700
Yeah, I think it was sort of like acting is casting.
是啊，我觉得演戏就像选角一样。

176
00:08:03.960 --> 00:08:04.720
You know what I mean?
你懂我的意思吗？

177
00:08:05.280 --> 00:08:07.540
I think it was just, like, kind of me.
我觉得他们就是想要我本人。

178
00:08:08.420 --> 00:08:14.520
And, I mean, that was why, you know, because a lot of people said, like, oh, like, did they want to name you Clark?
我是说，这就是为什么，很多人问，哦，他们是想让你叫克拉克吗？

179
00:08:14.700 --> 00:08:17.100
And, like, that was my idea.
那其实是我的主意。

180
00:08:17.100 --> 00:08:19.000
And it was sort of also in the back of my head, too.
我脑子里当时也隐约有这个想法。

181
00:08:19.120 --> 00:08:21.020
Like, maybe this is Clark from Clark and Michael.
就像是，也许这就是《克拉克和迈克尔》里的那个克拉克。

182
00:08:21.640 --> 00:08:23.260
Like, to, like, 10 years later or whatever.
十年后什么的。

183
00:08:23.580 --> 00:08:23.780
Yeah.
是啊。

184
00:08:24.020 --> 00:08:26.340
And, I mean, that was just, like, the lore in my head.
我是说，那只是我脑子里的背景设定。

185
00:08:26.440 --> 00:08:27.700
Like, not, like, you know, anybody else.
并不是说别人也这么想。

186
00:08:27.700 --> 00:08:32.100
But I also thought it was fun, you know, because there's a lot of people on the show that use their real name.
但我还觉得挺有趣的，因为剧里很多人都用自己的真名。

187
00:08:32.620 --> 00:08:36.320
I don't think there was a lot of specific, like, you need to play it like this.
我不觉得他们有什么具体要求，比如你必须怎么演。

188
00:08:36.440 --> 00:08:42.340
It was more, like, I think they kind of just wanted my, you know, me, whatever that is.
更多的是，我觉得他们只是想要我，你知道，就是我本人，不管那是什么样。

189
00:08:42.600 --> 00:08:46.200
I have one more, like, follow-up question to your casting process.
关于你的选角过程，我还有一个后续问题。

190
00:08:46.700 --> 00:08:54.220
At the time, weren't you told that this could possibly be, like, the beginning of a spinoff show?
当时，他们没告诉你这可能是衍生剧的开端吗？

191
00:08:54.540 --> 00:09:05.780
Like, that you and Jake were going to be the two new guys for the final season of The Office and that your characters might carry the torch into the next iteration?
就是说，你和杰克将成为《办公室》最终季的两位新人，而且你们的角色可能会接棒开启下一季？

192
00:09:06.140 --> 00:09:07.780
Yeah, that was my understanding of it.
是啊，我当时就是这么理解的。

193
00:09:07.960 --> 00:09:11.740
Not even, like, a spinoff, but, like, ER, you know, where it was, like, just new cats.
甚至都不算衍生剧，就像《急诊室的故事》那样，你知道，就是换一批新人。

194
00:09:11.820 --> 00:09:16.820
Some of the existing cats would stay and then you'd bring in, like, new people, too, and kind of be a mix.
保留一些老角色，再加入一些新人，形成一种混合模式。

195
00:09:16.940 --> 00:09:20.960
But, yeah, that was my understanding of it was it would be, yeah, like, ER.
但没错，我当时确实是那样理解的，就像《急诊室的故事》一样。

196
00:09:20.960 --> 00:09:21.500
Yeah.
是啊。

197
00:09:21.600 --> 00:09:22.540
And they would keep the show going.
他们想让这部剧继续下去。

198
00:09:23.000 --> 00:09:26.920
So, I mean, I was looking forward to being on the show for, like, years, you know, potentially.
所以，我是说，我本来期待着能在这部剧里演上好几年，你知道，很有可能。

199
00:09:27.340 --> 00:09:32.840
I remember when we watched the finale, there was all of this extra footage of you and Dakota.
我记得我们看大结局的时候，里面有很多你和达科塔的额外镜头。

200
00:09:33.020 --> 00:09:34.100
Dakota Johnson, yeah.
达科塔·约翰逊，没错。

201
00:09:34.100 --> 00:09:36.500
Yeah, and, like, you were going to be each other's love intereSt.
对，而且你们本来是要演对方的恋爱对象的。

202
00:09:36.540 --> 00:09:36.840
Right.
没错。

203
00:09:37.760 --> 00:09:41.600
We shot, like, this whole, I remember for, like, a week or two, we shot all this stuff.
我们拍了，大概，我记得拍了一两周，拍了好多素材。

204
00:09:41.740 --> 00:09:42.800
There's tons of footage.
有海量的镜头。

205
00:09:42.880 --> 00:09:43.800
Yeah, all gone.
对，全都没了。

206
00:09:43.960 --> 00:09:46.240
I wonder if they'll put it back in the superfan episode.
我在想他们会不会把这些放回超级粉丝版剧集里。

207
00:09:46.840 --> 00:09:47.200
Maybe.
也许吧。

208
00:09:47.200 --> 00:09:47.520
Maybe.
也许。

209
00:09:47.700 --> 00:09:54.100
Well, it was so funny, too, because I saw, like, or somebody sent it to me on Instagram a while ago when she was doing the press for a movie.
这事儿挺逗的，因为我之前在Instagram上看到，或者有人发给我看，当时她在为一部电影做宣传。

210
00:09:54.220 --> 00:09:57.960
She kept talking about how, like, oh, that was, like, the worst week of my life.
她一直在说，噢，那简直是我人生中最糟糕的一周。

211
00:09:58.040 --> 00:10:02.100
Like, I sit around and then they never used any of it, which made me laugh really hard.
就像是，我坐在那儿拍了半天，结果他们根本没用，这让我笑得不行。

212
00:10:02.260 --> 00:10:04.180
Well, Dakota, it might be in a superfan.
嗯，达科塔，也许它会出现在超级粉丝版里。

213
00:10:04.380 --> 00:10:05.320
It might come back.
它可能会重见天日。

214
00:10:05.320 --> 00:10:06.320
It might live again.
它可能会再次复活。

215
00:10:06.540 --> 00:10:11.520
But, yeah, but that was, yeah, that was my understanding of it and my hope, you know, to be honeSt.
不过，对，说实话，这就是我的理解，也是我的希望。

216
00:10:12.060 --> 00:10:17.260
Well, we have a fan question for you from Joanne Kay in Cape May, New Jersey.
好了，我们有一个来自新泽西州开普梅的乔安妮·凯的粉丝提问。

217
00:10:17.980 --> 00:10:22.240
She says, what was it like coming into the office so late in the run?
她问，在剧集后期才加入办公室是什么感觉？

218
00:10:22.360 --> 00:10:25.440
It seems like it would feel like being a transfer student senior year.
感觉就像高三才转学过去的学生一样吧？

219
00:10:25.860 --> 00:10:27.300
It was a little bit like that.
确实有点像那样。

220
00:10:27.480 --> 00:10:32.540
But, you know, the thing is, it wasn't hard because it was such a, like, smooth running machine.
但你知道，关键是，这并不难，因为它已经是一台运转非常顺畅的机器了。

221
00:10:32.940 --> 00:10:37.400
You know, you're joining, like, this thing that, like, runs like a clock at that point.
你知道，你加入的是一个在那个阶段已经像时钟一样精准运行的系统。

222
00:10:37.400 --> 00:10:39.040
And everybody was so nice.
而且每个人都特别好。

223
00:10:39.200 --> 00:10:41.860
And I will say you guys, specifically you two were the nicest of.
我得说，你们俩，尤其是你们俩，是其中最好的人。

224
00:10:42.000 --> 00:10:44.040
And I'm not just saying that because of the podcaSt.
我这么说可不仅仅是因为在录播客。

225
00:10:44.240 --> 00:10:45.580
You guys were very sweet to me.
你们对我真的非常好。

226
00:10:45.620 --> 00:10:46.740
I always appreciated it.
我一直很感激。

227
00:10:46.880 --> 00:10:50.120
We were very excited when you and Jake joined the show.
你和杰克加入剧组时我们特别兴奋。

228
00:10:50.300 --> 00:10:55.920
When we spoke with him, we told him that it was, like, we needed new people.
我们和他聊天时就说，我们需要新鲜血液。

229
00:10:56.080 --> 00:10:58.200
We were, you guys were so funny.
你们当时太搞笑了。

230
00:10:58.200 --> 00:10:59.400
You were so nice.
你们人太好了。

231
00:10:59.440 --> 00:11:00.600
You were so talented.
你们太有才了。

232
00:11:00.900 --> 00:11:03.040
You had new stories to tell.
你们有新的故事可以讲。

233
00:11:03.160 --> 00:11:07.000
Well, that's, I think that's the thing, too, is, like, we were like a family.
嗯，我觉得关键也在于，我们就像一家人一样。

234
00:11:07.000 --> 00:11:11.080
We're like, as soon as John started doing a bit, I'm like, that's his boom operator bit.
我们就像是，约翰一演那个梗，我就知道，那是他的收音师梗。

235
00:11:11.140 --> 00:11:12.480
We've seen it for nine years.
我们看了九年了。

236
00:11:12.780 --> 00:11:13.400
It's still funny.
但依然很好笑。

237
00:11:13.540 --> 00:11:16.200
But you guys came in with all this new energy.
不过你们带来了全新的活力。

238
00:11:16.500 --> 00:11:24.760
Well, it is very much like a family because, I mean, when you, you know, just from doing so much TV over the years, over the course of my life, like, you know,
嗯，确实非常像一家人，因为，我是说，当你，你知道，仅仅是因为我人生中这么多年拍了这么多电视剧，你知道，

239
00:11:24.900 --> 00:11:30.320
you spend more time with those people on set than you do, like, your actual family in a lot of cases.
在很多情况下，你和片场那些人待在一起的时间比和你真正的家人待在一起的时间还要长。

240
00:11:30.320 --> 00:11:36.760
Just, you know, for, like, six or nine months a year, like, 12 or 14 hours a day, like, it does, it is really like a family atmosphere.
就是，你知道，一年里有六到九个月，每天工作12到14个小时，确实，那真的是一种家庭氛围。

241
00:11:37.260 --> 00:11:45.500
So, yeah, it was sort of, I thought it was going to be intimidating, but it ended up being kind of just a pleasure because it was just so easy.
所以，对，我本来以为会很紧张，但结果却是一种享受，因为一切都太顺了。

242
00:11:45.600 --> 00:11:53.500
And everybody could go, you know, like, I remember, I think the first scene I ever shot was, it was me and Rain at, like, the snack machine.
每个人都能，你知道，我记得我拍的第一场戏，是我和雷恩在自动售货机那儿。

243
00:11:53.620 --> 00:11:54.360
Oh, my gosh.
天哪。

244
00:11:54.360 --> 00:11:59.720
And it was sort of, like, a feeling out thing of, like, because I wasn't sure how much, you know, like, how much improv to do.
那感觉有点像是在试探，因为我不确定，你知道，该做多少即兴表演。

245
00:11:59.780 --> 00:12:01.480
Like, you didn't want to show up and be, like.
你不想一上来就表现得像。

246
00:12:02.240 --> 00:12:02.800
That guy.
那种人。

247
00:12:03.220 --> 00:12:04.180
Yeah, yeah, yeah.
对，对，对。

248
00:12:04.240 --> 00:12:05.800
You don't want to, like, come in super hot.
你不想表现得太急于求成。

249
00:12:05.980 --> 00:12:07.180
Be like, I got jokes, guys.
别表现得像，嘿伙计们，我这儿有段子。

250
00:12:07.460 --> 00:12:10.260
I know you've won some Emmys, but hey, here's my stuff.
我知道你们拿过艾美奖，但嘿，看看我的表演。

251
00:12:10.380 --> 00:12:14.300
And, you know, like, it never needed a lot of improv because the scripts were so good, too.
而且，你知道，基本上不需要太多即兴发挥，因为剧本本身就写得太好了。

252
00:12:14.300 --> 00:12:19.140
But I remember, you know, being a little bit nervous, like, that day.
但我记得，你知道，那天我还是有点紧张的。

253
00:12:20.360 --> 00:12:26.800
But then it was just, you know, Rain is so funny, and me and him had a good, I felt like had good chemistry together, too.
但后来发现，你知道，Rain 真的太搞笑了，而且我觉得我和他之间也很有默契。

254
00:12:26.940 --> 00:12:28.260
So that was so easy.
所以一切都很顺利。

255
00:12:28.740 --> 00:12:30.600
I can't believe that was your first scene.
真不敢相信那是你的第一场戏。

256
00:12:30.720 --> 00:12:31.760
I'm pretty sure, yeah.
我很确定，是的。

257
00:12:32.520 --> 00:12:35.480
You guys cracked up a lot, and it's in the bloopers.
你们当时笑场了很多次，花絮里都有。

258
00:12:35.880 --> 00:12:35.980
Yeah.
是啊。

259
00:12:35.980 --> 00:12:37.500
And I actually was going to play it.
其实我本来打算放出来的。

260
00:12:37.980 --> 00:12:38.380
Ready?
准备好了吗？

261
00:12:38.580 --> 00:12:38.980
Are you ready?
你准备好了吗？

262
00:12:39.260 --> 00:12:41.940
This is, you guys are so tickled.
这简直，你们俩当时都被戳中笑点了。

263
00:12:42.260 --> 00:12:43.820
So, all right, here we go.
好了，我们要开始了。

264
00:12:44.400 --> 00:12:45.120
You want a coffee?
你想喝咖啡吗？

265
00:12:45.320 --> 00:12:47.680
No, I'll probably just finish the bag of shit.
不用，我大概会把那袋垃圾吃完。

266
00:12:47.940 --> 00:12:49.740
Again, you don't have to give me stuff.
再说一次，你没必要给我东西。

267
00:12:49.900 --> 00:12:50.520
I appreciate it, though.
不过我心领了。

268
00:12:50.600 --> 00:12:51.540
I got some noodles in my car.
我车里有些面条。

269
00:12:57.700 --> 00:12:59.180
Sorry, I'm cracking myself up, Greg.
抱歉，我把自己逗笑了，格雷格。

270
00:13:00.520 --> 00:13:01.160
Thank you, I mean...
谢谢你，我是说……

271
00:13:01.160 --> 00:13:05.040
I got some noodles in my car, so we could juSt...
我车里有些面条，所以我们可以……

272
00:13:07.040 --> 00:13:07.980
Just go get in your car?
就去你车里？

273
00:13:08.540 --> 00:13:10.840
I got some noodles in my car, we could just hang out and have some noodles.
我车里有些面条，我们可以待在那儿吃点面条。

274
00:13:15.260 --> 00:13:17.840
Jane, if you're more hungry, I got a big tub of noodles in my car.
简，如果你还饿的话，我车里有一大桶面条。

275
00:13:20.130 --> 00:13:20.810
Get it out.
把它拿出来。

276
00:13:22.150 --> 00:13:22.950
This goes on.
这还没完呢。

277
00:13:22.950 --> 00:13:23.710
Super professional.
超级专业。

278
00:13:23.910 --> 00:13:25.410
This goes on for a few minutes.
这持续了好几分钟。

279
00:13:26.030 --> 00:13:29.910
Literally every time you said, I got some noodles, you guys would start breaking.
真的，每次你说“我车里有些面条”的时候，你们俩就开始笑场。

280
00:13:29.910 --> 00:13:31.030
We basically just met.
我们当时基本才刚认识。

281
00:13:31.290 --> 00:13:32.530
Yeah, that is so fun, though.
是啊，不过那真的很有趣。

282
00:13:32.590 --> 00:13:35.090
You could already see the chemistry between the two characters.
你已经能看出这两个角色之间的化学反应了。

283
00:13:35.450 --> 00:13:44.510
Yeah, the hardest I've ever laughed, and the one that's still, like, if I catch it on TV, like, I don't know if you guys know this, but the show airs a lot on cable.
是啊，那是我笑得最厉害的一次，而且直到现在，如果我在电视上看到那一集——我不知道你们知不知道，但这剧在有线电视上重播率很高。

284
00:13:44.830 --> 00:13:45.810
It does, yes.
确实，没错。

285
00:13:45.810 --> 00:13:47.770
Um, so I, I see a lot.
嗯，所以我经常能看到。

286
00:13:48.510 --> 00:13:48.990
Yeah.
是啊。

287
00:13:49.290 --> 00:13:52.450
Yeah, like on Comedy Central, and every, every channel.
对，比如在喜剧中心频道，还有各种频道。

288
00:13:52.630 --> 00:13:53.810
It seems to be on every channel.
它好像在每个频道都在播。

289
00:13:53.810 --> 00:13:54.250
It's on a loop.
简直是在循环播放。

290
00:13:54.570 --> 00:14:00.750
Um, but if I ever see the one where we're trying to move Stanley's body.
嗯，但如果我看到我们试图搬运斯坦利尸体的那一集。

291
00:14:01.710 --> 00:14:02.770
Down the stairs.
从楼梯上搬下去。

292
00:14:02.790 --> 00:14:03.430
Down the stairs.
从楼梯上搬下去。

293
00:14:04.270 --> 00:14:04.750
Starmageddon.
“斯坦利末日”。

294
00:14:05.830 --> 00:14:11.790
That, to me, like, I, like, I, even, like, shooting, I, like, could not hold it, like, none of, I could not hold it together.
那对我来说，真的，我，甚至在拍摄的时候，我都完全忍不住，根本控制不住自己。

295
00:14:11.810 --> 00:14:15.990
I was, like, this is the funniest, like, when his head launches into the wall.
我当时觉得，这太搞笑了，尤其是当他的头撞进墙里的时候。

296
00:14:16.050 --> 00:14:16.570
Into the wall.
撞进墙里。

297
00:14:16.770 --> 00:14:17.150
Because that was.
因为那确实是。

298
00:14:17.290 --> 00:14:18.090
Oh, my gosh.
天哪。

299
00:14:18.450 --> 00:14:27.330
Because it was, but that was, that was the great thing about the show and about, um, you know, and about mockumentary is the, you know,
因为那是，但那正是这部剧的伟大之处，关于，嗯，你知道，关于伪纪录片形式的，你知道，

300
00:14:27.390 --> 00:14:30.970
the formula and the format of the show being so grounded with the mockumentary.
这部剧的公式和形式，因为伪纪录片风格而显得非常真实接地气。

301
00:14:31.110 --> 00:14:33.270
You can get away with really big, broad stuff.
你可以尝试非常夸张、大开大合的东西。

302
00:14:33.830 --> 00:14:36.210
Because I was, like, at first, I was, like, this is really silly.
因为我起初觉得，这太傻了。

303
00:14:36.350 --> 00:14:37.730
Like, I don't know if this is going to work at all.
就像，我不知道这到底能不能行得通。

304
00:14:38.030 --> 00:14:42.930
But then you watch it and it totally works because, like, the, you know, the mockumentary thing grounds it.
但当你看着看着，它就完全行得通了，因为伪纪录片的形式让它有了现实感。

305
00:14:43.450 --> 00:14:51.310
Um, but yeah, that, that was, that's, I still think about that and laugh, uh, just trying to shoot that and get through it because, like, nobody could keep it together.
嗯，不过确实，那件事，我到现在想起来还会笑，当时拍的时候大家都在努力忍住不笑，因为根本没人能绷得住。

306
00:14:52.090 --> 00:15:03.250
I love that you brought that up because, um, I feel like we were afraid to do that mix of, like, a broad concept and then, like, but keeping it in the mockumentary.
很高兴你提到了这一点，因为我觉得我们之前很担心把这种夸张的概念和伪纪录片的形式结合在一起。

307
00:15:03.270 --> 00:15:13.650
And it was Mindy's episode, The Injury, where Michael grills his foot, which is just such, like, a broad, ridiculous idea.
那是明迪编剧的一集《受伤》，迈克尔把脚烫伤了，这主意简直太夸张、太荒唐了。

308
00:15:14.250 --> 00:15:19.610
And after that episode worked, I felt like that, the writers were, like, oh, okay.
在那一集成功之后，我觉得编剧们意识到，噢，原来可以这样。

309
00:15:19.910 --> 00:15:20.150
Yeah.
没错。

310
00:15:20.390 --> 00:15:20.690
Okay.
好的。

311
00:15:21.050 --> 00:15:22.430
We see what we can do here.
我们知道在这里能做什么了。

312
00:15:22.810 --> 00:15:25.150
Meredith can have a bat attack her head.
梅雷迪思可以被蝙蝠袭击头部。

313
00:15:25.990 --> 00:15:26.390
Yes.
没错。

314
00:15:26.390 --> 00:15:28.010
Or get hit by Michael's car.
或者被迈克尔的车撞到。

315
00:15:28.130 --> 00:15:28.290
Yeah.
是啊。

316
00:15:28.310 --> 00:15:28.970
It really does, though.
确实是这样。

317
00:15:28.970 --> 00:15:33.830
It gives you, it gives you a lot of freedom because, um, I mean, just think, I mean, even think of, like, spinal tap.
它给了你很大的自由度，因为，想想看，哪怕想想《摇滚万万岁》那种片子。

318
00:15:34.230 --> 00:15:34.630
Yes.
没错。

319
00:15:43.650 --> 00:15:50.990
Like, I did it in Clark and Michael and then, uh, did it in The Office, but, um, yeah, I'd love to do more mockumentary.
我在《克拉克与迈克尔》里用过这种手法，后来在《办公室》里也用过，但我确实很想再拍些伪纪录片。

320
00:15:51.330 --> 00:15:53.550
Well, you're a writer-director now.
好吧，你现在是编剧兼导演了。

321
00:15:53.990 --> 00:15:54.390
That's true.
确实。

322
00:15:54.390 --> 00:15:56.690
Would you ever go that route?
你会考虑走那条路吗？

323
00:15:56.910 --> 00:16:01.750
I actually have a script I'm working on right now that I would like to try to shoot this year that's a mockumentary, yeah.
我手头确实有个剧本正在写，我想今年试着拍出来，那是一部伪纪录片。

324
00:16:01.890 --> 00:16:03.470
But I don't know if I'm going to be in it.
但我不知道自己会不会在里面出演。

325
00:16:03.810 --> 00:16:04.150
Mm-hmm.
嗯。

326
00:16:04.150 --> 00:16:06.110
Uh, but, but, yeah, definitely.
嗯，不过，绝对会考虑的。

327
00:16:06.610 --> 00:16:10.010
Just because I miss, I miss, like, it's such, and it's such a fun way to shoot, too.
只是因为我很怀念那种感觉，而且这种拍摄方式真的很有趣。

328
00:16:10.210 --> 00:16:10.590
Mm-hmm.
嗯。

329
00:16:10.870 --> 00:16:12.590
Um, you know, you can move so faSt.
你知道，拍摄节奏可以非常快。

330
00:16:12.790 --> 00:16:18.410
Like, that was the other crazy thing about The Office is how it felt like we shot a ton of pages a day.
《办公室》另一件疯狂的事就是我们每天要拍海量的剧本页数。

331
00:16:19.190 --> 00:16:19.670
We did.
确实如此。

332
00:16:19.930 --> 00:16:20.190
Yeah, we did.
是啊，我们做到了。

333
00:16:20.390 --> 00:16:22.950
Yeah, like, compared to other stuff, like, um.
比起其他作品，真的。

334
00:16:23.390 --> 00:16:24.930
So much, like, yeah, like, I'll.
太多了，真的。

335
00:16:25.090 --> 00:16:28.090
Like, 10 or 12 plus pages a day, which is a lot.
每天拍10到12页以上，这非常多。

336
00:16:28.190 --> 00:16:29.490
I don't, I mean, I don't know if, like, people know, like.
我不知道大家是否了解这一点。

337
00:16:29.970 --> 00:16:30.530
That's a lot.
那真的很多。

338
00:16:30.670 --> 00:16:31.510
It's a lot of pages, yeah.
确实是很多页，没错。

339
00:16:31.510 --> 00:16:32.210
It's a lot of pages.
页数非常多。

340
00:16:32.210 --> 00:16:39.770
And also, you know, we didn't move our lighting once we were in that main bullpen, so we didn't have to wait for a lot of setups so we could move really quickly.
而且，你知道，一旦我们在那个主办公区，灯光就不用动了，所以我们不需要花时间等布光，拍摄速度非常快。

341
00:16:39.950 --> 00:16:43.290
Which was great, because as an actor, you, you kept the energy up.
这太棒了，因为作为演员，你可以一直保持那种能量。

342
00:16:43.630 --> 00:16:43.750
Yeah.
没错。

343
00:16:43.910 --> 00:16:44.090
Totally.
完全同意。

344
00:16:44.390 --> 00:16:48.030
Uh, you wouldn't have that sort of slump as they would take forever to light.
你不会因为漫长的布光等待而感到疲惫。

345
00:16:48.290 --> 00:16:55.670
But I remember after being on The Office and going through, like, 10, 12 pages a day, going to shoot a movie, and I would look at the call sheet, and I'd be like,
但我记得在拍完《办公室》之后，习惯了每天拍10到12页，再去拍电影时，我看着通告单心想，

346
00:16:55.750 --> 00:16:57.990
we're doing seven-eighths of a page today.
我们今天只拍七分之八页？

347
00:16:58.170 --> 00:16:59.250
Yeah, like, one or two pages, yeah.
是啊，一两页而已，没错。

348
00:16:59.330 --> 00:16:59.570
Yeah.
是啊。

349
00:17:00.210 --> 00:17:01.390
I was like, oh, okay.
我当时就想，噢，好吧。

350
00:17:01.390 --> 00:17:02.830
Yeah, it's a lot of sitting around.
没错，大部分时间都在干坐着。

351
00:17:03.090 --> 00:17:08.470
We're going to do this one page for 12 hours, as opposed to 12 pages in 12 hours.
我们要用12个小时拍这一页，而不是用12个小时拍12页。

352
00:17:08.950 --> 00:17:10.410
It's, it's great as an actor.
作为演员，这感觉太棒了。

353
00:17:10.710 --> 00:17:16.010
I mean, the mock-up-anything, too, because you're shooting with, you know, two or three cameras usually at all times, too, so you can, you know, kind of,
我的意思是，那种模拟一切的感觉也很好，因为你通常总是用两三台摄像机同时拍摄，所以你可以，你知道，有点像，

354
00:17:16.510 --> 00:17:19.650
like a Robert Altman thing, like, talk over each other and not have to worry about that.
就像罗伯特·奥特曼的风格，大家可以同时说话，而不必担心（收音问题）。

355
00:17:19.750 --> 00:17:20.170
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

356
00:17:20.170 --> 00:17:21.690
Um, yeah, I loved it.
嗯，是的，我喜欢这种方式。

357
00:17:22.110 --> 00:17:22.370
Yeah.
是的。

358
00:17:22.930 --> 00:17:28.510
Well, looking back on The Office, is there a particular moment or episode that stands out to you as one of your favorites?
那么，回顾《办公室》，有没有哪个特定的时刻或剧集让你印象深刻，成为你的最爱之一？

359
00:17:29.230 --> 00:17:30.330
I mean, Stairmageddon.
我是说，《楼梯末日》那一集。

360
00:17:30.450 --> 00:17:37.770
I already answered this one, but that, that episode, um, and, and the first one, the first one where you meet us, you know, was obviously a really special thing for me.
我之前回答过这个问题，但那一集，嗯，还有第一集，就是你们第一次见到我们的那一集，对我来说显然是非常特别的。

361
00:17:37.770 --> 00:17:43.030
Well, you know what, um, the one where, where Dwight takes me on the sales call when we go to the father-son.
嗯，你知道吗，嗯，就是德怀特带我去参加销售拜访，我们去那对父子那儿的那一集。

362
00:17:43.330 --> 00:17:44.630
Is that Suit Warehouse?
是《西装仓库》那一集吗？

363
00:17:44.810 --> 00:17:45.130
Yes.
是的。

364
00:17:45.270 --> 00:17:45.530
Yes.
没错。

365
00:17:45.710 --> 00:17:46.570
It's so good.
那集太棒了。

366
00:17:46.710 --> 00:17:47.990
That episode is so good.
那集真的太棒了。

367
00:17:48.330 --> 00:17:53.970
That, that, that might have been, that was a really fun one to shoot, uh, for me, just because the stuff with Ryan was so fun.
那，那，那可能，那对我来说拍起来真的很有趣，只是因为和瑞安演对手戏太好玩了。

368
00:17:53.970 --> 00:18:03.170
And, I mean, the most surreal one, or the, the one that, like, maybe sticks out the most was, um, the finale, just because that was a little surreal.
而且，我是说，最超现实的一集，或者说，最让我印象深刻的，是结局那一集，因为那感觉有点超现实。

369
00:18:03.310 --> 00:18:06.310
Like, talk about the, like, transferring, like, senior year somewhere.
就像是，谈论那种，转学到某个地方读大四的感觉。

370
00:18:06.470 --> 00:18:08.670
Like, and me and Jake Lacey have talked about this.
就像，我和杰克·莱西聊过这个。

371
00:18:08.790 --> 00:18:14.270
Like, it was, it was kind of surreal because, you know, you guys had all been together so long and everybody's, like, crying and hugging.
就像，这感觉有点，有点超现实，因为，你知道，你们大家在一起待了那么久，每个人都在哭，都在拥抱。

372
00:18:14.510 --> 00:18:16.610
But we kind of felt like two guys, like, standing around.
但我们感觉就像两个站在旁边的人。

373
00:18:16.750 --> 00:18:22.130
Like, you feel kind of like, you know, you feel a little, like, like, like, weird, like, like, you're at, like, the funeral of someone.
就像，你感觉有点，你知道，你感觉有点，有点，有点奇怪，就像，就像你在参加某人的葬礼。

374
00:18:22.210 --> 00:18:22.330
Yeah.
是的。

375
00:18:23.970 --> 00:18:24.470
Like, what do I do?
就像，我该做什么？

376
00:18:24.790 --> 00:18:25.970
Like, an acquaintance's funeral, you know?
就像，一个熟人的葬礼，你知道吗？

377
00:18:26.150 --> 00:18:26.370
Yeah.
是的。

378
00:18:26.670 --> 00:18:29.270
So that was, that was the most surreal thing, probably.
所以那大概是最超现实的事情了。

379
00:18:30.070 --> 00:18:33.190
But, yeah, funniest one is Stairmageddon for me.
不过，是的，对我来说最搞笑的是《楼梯末日》那一集。

380
00:18:33.510 --> 00:18:34.730
Like, just could not keep it together.
简直笑得停不下来。

381
00:18:34.930 --> 00:18:41.730
And then, yeah, the first, the, for the first episode of that season where they introduced us and then, um, yeah, probably a suit warehouse.
还有，是的，那一季的第一集，他们介绍我们出场的时候，然后，嗯，是的，大概就是《西装仓库》那一集。

382
00:18:42.470 --> 00:18:44.950
Well, you have one of my favorite talking heads.
嗯，你有一个我最喜欢的“访谈”片段。

383
00:18:45.110 --> 00:18:47.870
It's when Clark is talking about his weekend with Jan.
就是克拉克谈论他和简度过的那个周末。

384
00:18:48.710 --> 00:18:51.050
And it's one of my absolute favorites.
那绝对是我最喜欢的片段之一。

385
00:18:51.350 --> 00:18:52.350
And I want to play it.
我想放出来看看。

386
00:18:52.490 --> 00:18:52.670
Okay.
好的。

387
00:18:53.350 --> 00:18:54.130
Hey, guys.
嘿，伙计们。

388
00:18:54.750 --> 00:18:55.790
Clark, hey.
克拉克，嘿。

389
00:18:56.150 --> 00:18:57.430
Hey, look who's back.
嘿，看谁回来了。

390
00:18:57.550 --> 00:18:57.970
Dwight Jr.
小德怀特。

391
00:18:58.370 --> 00:18:59.690
Hey, so how was it?
嘿，感觉怎么样？

392
00:18:59.910 --> 00:19:02.570
I mean, the sex with Jan.
我是说，和简的那种事。

393
00:19:02.970 --> 00:19:07.650
A gentleman doesn't discuss such matters, especially when the feelings of a lady are involved.
绅士是不会讨论这种事情的，尤其是当涉及到女士的感受时。

394
00:19:07.850 --> 00:19:10.750
Women reach their sexual peak at whatever age Jan was last week.
女性在简上周那个年纪时达到了性欲巅峰。

395
00:19:11.170 --> 00:19:14.430
I mean, it was like making love with a wild animal.
我的意思是，那感觉就像是在和一只野生动物做爱。

396
00:19:15.830 --> 00:19:17.090
But not like a cougar.
但不是像美洲狮那样的。

397
00:19:17.350 --> 00:19:20.950
Like you might think it was, uh, like a swarm of bees.
就像你可能以为的那样，呃，就像一群蜜蜂。

398
00:19:23.050 --> 00:19:25.990
Bees that just find something wrong with every hotel room.
一群对每个酒店房间都能挑出毛病的蜜蜂。

399
00:19:28.790 --> 00:19:29.550
That's a good one.
那段真不错。

400
00:19:29.550 --> 00:19:30.510
That is so good.
那真的太棒了。

401
00:19:31.070 --> 00:19:32.710
Your delivery is so great.
你的演绎太棒了。

402
00:19:33.670 --> 00:19:34.030
Yeah.
是啊。

403
00:19:34.230 --> 00:19:35.170
I did not write that line.
那句台词不是我写的。

404
00:19:35.290 --> 00:19:35.770
I wish I did.
我倒希望是我写的。

405
00:19:35.910 --> 00:19:37.330
That's, that's excellent.
那真的很棒。

406
00:19:39.430 --> 00:19:41.310
That was a funny storyline in general.
总的来说，那条故事线很有趣。

407
00:19:41.410 --> 00:19:48.770
Because I think, if I remember right, I think that was sort of, um, the me and Jan thing was sort of written in because I had to go shoot a movie.
因为我觉得，如果我没记错的话，我和简（Jan）的那段剧情之所以被写进去，是因为我当时要去拍一部电影。

408
00:19:48.770 --> 00:19:52.650
And it was one of those deals where, like, I was committed to that before I came on the show.
那是那种我在加入剧组之前就已经签好的合约。

409
00:19:52.670 --> 00:19:54.270
So, like, we had to carve it out type of deal.
所以，我们得想办法把那段戏给挤出来。

410
00:19:54.390 --> 00:19:54.630
Sure.
确实。

411
00:19:55.130 --> 00:19:58.230
I think that was why the Jan thing was, was how they wrote, wrote me off.
我想这就是为什么他们会用简的那条线来让我退出剧组。

412
00:19:58.350 --> 00:19:59.950
But, yeah, what a great, funny way to do it.
不过，说真的，这真是一个又棒又好笑的处理方式。

413
00:20:00.050 --> 00:20:00.270
Yeah.
是啊。

414
00:20:00.510 --> 00:20:01.250
For, like, three weeks.
大概持续了三周吧。

415
00:20:01.670 --> 00:20:05.270
Do you have any, like, offset behind-the-scenes memories?
你有什么幕后的花絮记忆吗？

416
00:20:05.410 --> 00:20:09.030
Like, when you look back at that time on The Office, what do you think of?
比如，当你回首在《办公室》的那段时光，你会想到什么？

417
00:20:09.430 --> 00:20:10.270
I mean, it was, I don't know.
我是说，我不知道。

418
00:20:10.290 --> 00:20:11.050
It was an interesting time.
那是一段有趣的时光。

419
00:20:11.190 --> 00:20:13.950
Like, I mean, I'm trying to think of stuff that would not be interesting to talk about.
我是说，我在想有什么事情是不值得拿出来说的。

420
00:20:14.070 --> 00:20:18.750
Because, I mean, for me, it's like, I think about, you know, like, it felt like kind of a transitional moment in my life.
因为对我来说，我觉得那是我人生中一个转折点。

421
00:20:18.770 --> 00:20:19.630
Like, I was moving.
比如，我当时在搬家。

422
00:20:19.810 --> 00:20:24.510
Like, I literally just moved from, so where they tape here, the podcast, I used to live across the street in this building.
我刚从——就是我们现在录播客的这个地方，我以前就住在街对面的那栋楼里。

423
00:20:24.770 --> 00:20:28.050
And I had moved out of there and was, like, living in this, like, this house I rented.
我搬出了那里，住进了我现在租的这栋房子里。

424
00:20:28.890 --> 00:20:30.370
Yeah, we should share with everyone.
是啊，我们应该和大家分享一下。

425
00:20:30.690 --> 00:20:32.570
When you walked in, you were like, oh, my gosh.
你刚走进来的时候，你当时说，天哪。

426
00:20:32.750 --> 00:20:37.010
From the windows where we record, he can literally see the window of his old apartment.
从我们录音的窗户往外看，他真的能看到他以前公寓的窗户。

427
00:20:37.110 --> 00:20:39.030
Yeah, I can see my old apartment across the street here.
没错，我能看到街对面我以前住的公寓。

428
00:20:39.930 --> 00:20:40.630
Yes, I don't know.
是啊，我不知道该怎么说。

429
00:20:40.710 --> 00:20:44.830
So, for me, it was an interesting, it was such a fun, weird kind of year.
所以对我来说，那是非常有趣、非常快乐又奇妙的一年。

430
00:20:44.830 --> 00:20:52.650
Because it was like, you know, just being on the show felt like this fun gift, like, that was just put in my lap that I got to do for a year.
因为能参与这部剧感觉就像是一份上天赐予的礼物，让我有幸能做上一年。

431
00:20:52.790 --> 00:20:54.250
So, it was just kind of pure joy.
所以那段经历纯粹是快乐。

